11.0.0, twenty-first upload — the Instrument page, and audio in stereo

What is new since 10029. Each line is code that the Echoel Studio run builds and, where a test
target reaches it, tests; nothing here is device-verified yet.
- Instrument: the first chip in the bar. The Field on top, your pulse, Body Source, Body Voice,
  the tempo lock Fixed | Flow, Sound and Mood; the keys stay under the page.
- Body Voice: a Body track on a pad sound, silent until you switch it on. The keys play it;
  coherence opens and brightens its sound and your pulse sets its vibrato — three ordinary routes
  you can see and change under Modulate. Pulse, HRV and coherence are for self-observation.
- Flow: the tempo follows your pulse only through four stages — a steady reading for 5 s, folded
  into 60–160 BPM near the tempo that plays, at most 2 BPM per bar, gliding over 2 s — and only
  while the song plays. Never while a Jam host or a MIDI clock sets the tempo. Flow writes nothing
  into the song; switching back to Fixed keeps the tempo it reached, as one undo step.
- Vibrato is a new synth parameter, also in the plug-in (at the end of its list).
- Stereo: imported audio, regions, clips and Bake Effects keep left and right. Mono stays mono;
  more than two channels fold to stereo. Pan on a stereo region works as balance. A wide file can
  sound up to 3 dB louder than its former mono mix. Recording stays mono.

Previous: 11.0.0 (10029), twentieth upload — the Jam starts together on the next bar. 10028 and
earlier: see git history of this file.
group.com.echoelmusic is in the app's entitlements since a14e1960a (F17, 2026-10-21); the import
of earlier songs has not been seen on a device yet.

Bump this file on a commit whose "Echoel Studio" run is green to upload a build
(.github/workflows/studio-testflight.yml). Build number = 10000 + the workflow's run number.
The version is MARKETING_VERSION in EchoelStudio/project.yml.
This file is a test list for the device, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

Five things to try on the device (FOUNDER_INBOX rule 1: five per build; answer each yes or no):
1. A fingertip on the rear camera, open Instrument, Body Source: the camera, switch Body Voice on
   and play the keys. Breathe slowly and calmly for a minute: does the sound open and brighten,
   and does the vibrato follow your pulse?
2. Press Play on a song and set the tempo lock to Flow: the tempo field reads FLOW and the tempo
   moves slowly toward your pulse, bar by bar. Switch to Fixed: it stays where it got to, and
   Undo takes that back.
3. Import a stereo file with a sound only on the left, and play it: left stays left. Bake a
   region through Chorus: the baked track stays wide.
4. Two iPhones, Wi-Fi off, click on: one hosts, the other joins. The host presses Play in the
   middle of a bar: "Starting on the next bar.", both begin together on that bar, and the clicks
   still sound together after five minutes.
5. After trying Instrument: should Echoel open on Instrument instead of Tracks?
